hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan in today's  episode I'm going to answer a question  from one of my newsletter readers Anna  who is trying to raise fifteen to twenty  thousand dollars to create a new social  networking type of website and go after  investors and one of my advice on how to  do it so I know thanks for the question  I think for you it's a tough amount of  money to raise if you're looking only at  fifteen to twenty thousand  you're not really getting a serious  investor involved you know you're not  getting somebody who has a lot of  experience usually a lot of the angel  guys that would be too low an amount for  them so you might get somebody like a  dentist or a doctor to come in and you  know they have extra cash and would want  to invest but they may not have a lot of  experience and part of bringing money in  is you don't want just money you want  someone who can help you and give you  connections right they're gonna be part  of your ownership team they have equity  in your business so you want them to  give you more than just money you want  them to be a helpful resource for you so  you definitely want to qualify your  investors but it may be too little an  amount to go after a serious investor  the next thing is a lot of people want  to start social media sites so you know  this is this is gonna be a negative  hurdle for you to have to overcome  there's a there's a stigma that a lot of  the social media sites have already been  created and for you know new products or  services it's encouraged to build around  the existing social media sites instead  of trying to build your own new one from  scratch so there are still some examples  of one that have paid it big but deserve  there's a negative bias that you're  gonna have to overcome and really show  how you're different and what's so  unique about you and why you're gonna  make it where all these other you know  startup social media sites have failed I  think a more important issue is you're  raising money to bring on you know a  team to help you you know build this  website so some company that you've  hired to you know they've quoted you for  the website and you're gonna pay them to  do it it's really hard and from an  investor's point of view so I used to be  a venture capitalist  we wouldn't touch a business like this  because you don't have the technology  team in-house so for an investor they  want to see at some point that you're  going to be able to exit  from your business you're gonna be able  to pay them their money back so either  you're gonna go public we're gonna get  acquired or it's gonna be some kind of  management buyout and they look at what  kind of technology do you have in the  house and it's really hard to run a  business without having somebody on the  technology side in-house right  everything is exported to you know  overseas or some other company even if  they're local you don't have the  experience in-house and it's really hard  to grow business that way and really  hard to raise money for that type of  business so what I would encourage you  to do is try to find a partner who  really understands the technology side  of things can build it without having  you give up you know capital win over  the raise capital bring on a jewel  investor try to find a partner who's  committed to it and work around that if  you're able to build up a prototype and  get it going and get some momentum with  it then will be a lot easier to raise  money because you have somebody in-house  you have core competencies you have  intellectual property and you don't have  to keep paying outside companies to  finance your development so I hope that  helps they've been up to news you wanted  to hear but those are my thoughts if you  guys liked the video please give it a  thumbs up below it makes me want to make  more of these videos for you guys and  I'd love to hear you have to think if  you have some comments leave it below in  